speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, I rise on a question of privilege. I have never abused this procedure. I have been sitting here for ten years and I never used it before as far as I can remember. I simply refer to what the hon. member for Grenville-Carle-ton (Mr. Baker) said yesterday. I did not do this earlier because there was some confusion yesterday on the import of his words; then I read Hansard, and here is what the hon. member said. I shall say it in English because he spoke in English so that his words are not misinterpreted. The hon. member said the following, and I quote;

Again, a question to the Prime Minister. In view of the now public admission in the matter of the extension of the Sky Shops lease that the then minister of DREE was allowed input into the question as Quebec leader, although this lease-

Mr. Speaker, this is the point I want to raise this afternoon. I do not know where there was public admission that I played a role in the extension of the Sky Shops contract. I even stated the contrary; nobody ever dared state that I had something to do directly or indirectly with the Sky Shops affair. I hope that the hon. member did not think what he said and that he will simply say what he meant, and the matter will be settled. If he maintains that he did say this, Mr. Speaker, I will ask you to have him withdraw his words if he does not want the normal procedure in such a case to be followed. I do not want-and I have no intention of playing the offended virgin-reputations to be destroyed through insinuations; I think that we should not accept this in the House.
